--> Phase 1 — referential integrity for tenant scoping.
-->
--> 258 tables carry company_id; none declared a foreign key, so the database
--> enforced nothing and application code was the only thing keeping one
--> tenant out of another's rows. That is the right guard but not the only
--> writer: migrations, fixes and reports write directly.
-->
--> ON DELETE RESTRICT throughout — a company with records under it must not
--> be removable by accident. CASCADE would take the whole tenant silently.
-->
--> Four tables are deliberately absent: correspondence,
--> correspondence_recipients, number_sequences and risks hold 18 rows
--> pointing at company ids that never existed, left by earlier test runs.
--> The constraint is deferred rather than the rows deleted.
